<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕdīcŭlus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕdīclus</span></b> ),
			i, m.
		dim.
		pes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little foot.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pediculi octoni omnibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 28, 44, § 83</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argentei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 2, 33</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the foot-stalk</i>
			or <i>pedicle</i> of a fruit or leaf: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pediculi Punicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 44, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uvarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 43, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pediculo brevi sunt folia oleae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 24, 38, § 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fungorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					22, 23, 47, § 96</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
